  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday morning through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 200 PM EDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nExpect little change in the long-term forecast with a building \nmid-level ridge centered over Texas and associated troughing \noriented along the eastern seaboard, which will continue to \namplify through Friday and shift off the coast by the weekend. Dry\nconditions will continue to be the theme with no chance of rain \nthrough at least the end of next week. \n\nOtherwise, this pattern will reinforce the seasonably cooler \nconditions over our area through the first of next week. A \nresulting backdoor cold front will move through by Friday, \nincreasing surface winds out of the northeast to around 5-10mph, \nwith afternoon gusts up to 20mph through the weekend. Expect \novernight lows to drop into the low to upper 40s and daytime highs\nranging from the low 60s to upper 70s area wide this weekend. \nExpect a gradual warming trend as we move into the second half of \nnext week.",
